nsform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-D7\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> 10<sup>-5</sup> m. The maximum percentage error in the Young's\nmodulus of the wire is ","options":[],"correct_options":[],"explanation":"<p>The difference between the two measurements by Vernier scale gives elongation of the wire caused by the additional load of 2 kg. In the first measurement, main scale reading is MSR = 3.20 <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0.02ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.09ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -491 778 482\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-D7\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> 10<sup><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>2</sup> m and Vernier scale reading is VSR = 20. The least count of Vernier scale is LC = 1 <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0.02ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.09ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -491 778 482\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-D7\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> 10<sup><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>5</sup> m. Thus, the first measurement by Vernier scale is</p>\n<p>L<sub>1</sub> = MSR + VSR <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0.02ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.09ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -491 778 482\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-D7\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> LC</p>\n<p>= 3.20 <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0.02ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.09ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -491 778 482\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-D7\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> 10<sup><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505e